### Cluster S02-C1 — the ONE shared modal-semantics helper

Creates `apps/ui/components/consent/modalSemantics.ts` and `tests/render/consent-modal-semantics.test.tsx`.
**This is the mission's first artefact** (`SPEC.md` §Parallel-safety; `COMMON.md` §10.7):
S01's preferences card cannot satisfy S01-R18 or the Esc stack until it exists, and it
references no CSS token, so it needs nothing from the other lane.

**The module's exported surface, fixed here so C5/C6 and S01 can be written against it:**

```ts
export type ModalSurface = Readonly<{
  containerRef: React.RefObject<HTMLElement | null>;
  initialFocusRef: React.RefObject<HTMLElement | null>;
  onClose: () => void;
}>;
export function useModalSurface(open: boolean, surface: ModalSurface): void;
export function backdropCloseHandler(
  scrim: HTMLElement | null, onClose: () => void
): (event: { target: EventTarget | null }) => void;
export function prefersReducedMotion(): boolean;
export function openSurfaceCount(): number;   // test-visible depth of the Esc stack
```

- **S02-S01 · The Esc stack: one Escape, one surface, and it is the topmost.**
  Serves `SPEC.md` R16, R14, R08. Creates `apps/ui/components/consent/modalSemantics.ts` and
  `tests/render/consent-modal-semantics.test.tsx`.
  **Test:** mount two components through `useModalSurface`, outer first then inner; dispatch
  ONE `new KeyboardEvent("keydown", { key: "Escape", bubbles: true })` on `document` inside
  `act`. **Property:** the inner surface's `onClose` was called exactly once and the outer
  surface's `onClose` was called zero times.
  **RED before** (`Cannot find module '…/modalSemantics'` — the module this step creates),
  **GREEN after.**
  **Acceptance:** a stranger runs the C1 command and reads `Tests 1 passed (1)`; with the
  module's stack replaced by a per-surface listener, the same run reports the outer `onClose`
  called once and fails. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S02 · Initial focus lands on the element the caller names.**
  Serves R16. Edits `modalSemantics.ts`, `consent-modal-semantics.test.tsx`.
  **Test:** mount one surface whose `initialFocusRef` points at a `<button>` that is not first
  in DOM order. **Property:** after mount, `document.activeElement` is that button.
  **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 2 passed (2)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S03 · Focus returns to whatever was focused when the surface opened.**
  Serves R16, R07, R08. Edits both files.
  **Test:** focus a `<input id="opener">`, open the surface, then close it. **Property:**
  `document.activeElement` is `#opener` again. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:**
  `Tests 3 passed (3)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S04 · Tab from the last focusable inside the surface goes to the first.**
  Serves R16. Edits both files.
  **Test:** focus the last focusable, dispatch `keydown` `Tab` (no shift). **Property:**
  `document.activeElement` is the first focusable of that surface and
  `event.defaultPrevented` is `true`. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:**
  `Tests 4 passed (4)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S05 · Shift+Tab from the first focusable goes to the last.**
  Serves R16. Edits both files.
  **Test:** focus the first focusable, dispatch `keydown` `Tab` with `shiftKey: true`.
  **Property:** `document.activeElement` is the last focusable. **RED before, GREEN after.
  Acceptance:** `Tests 5 passed (5)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S06 · The focusable set is recomputed on every Tab, never cached at open.**
  Serves R16 (and the R15 interaction: `I have read it` is `disabled` at open and enabled
  later). Edits both files.
  **Test:** mount with a `disabled` trailing button; remove `disabled`; Tab from the last
  *enabled* control. **Property:** focus reaches the newly enabled button rather than wrapping
  past it. **RED before** (a cached list wraps to the first), **GREEN after. Acceptance:**
  `Tests 6 passed (6)`. Cluster **C1**.
  **Derivation of the focusable selector, pinned so C5/C6 do not re-derive it:**
  `a[href], button:not([disabled]), input:not([disabled]), select:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled]), [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])`.

- **S02-S07 · A backdrop click closes only when the click landed ON the backdrop.**
  Serves R14, R08. Edits both files.
  **Test:** call the handler returned by `backdropCloseHandler(scrim, onClose)` twice — once
  with `{ target: scrim }`, once with `{ target: aChildElement }`. **Property:** `onClose` was
  called exactly once, on the first. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:**
  `Tests 7 passed (7)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S08 · `prefersReducedMotion()` is safe when `matchMedia` does not exist.**
  Serves R24, R14. Edits both files.
  **Test:** with the jsdom default (**measured: `typeof window.matchMedia === "undefined"` in
  jsdom 30.0.1**) call it; then `vi.stubGlobal`-style assign a `matchMedia` returning
  `{ matches: true }` and call it again. **Property:** `false` in the first case with no throw,
  `true` in the second. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 8 passed (8)`.
  Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S09 · Closing the inner surface hands Escape back to the outer one.**
  Serves R16. Edits both files.
  **Test:** open outer, open inner, close inner, dispatch one Escape. **Property:** the outer
  surface's `onClose` is now called exactly once. **RED before** (a stack that never pops
  leaves the closed inner surface on top and swallows the key), **GREEN after. Acceptance:**
  `Tests 9 passed (9)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S10 · Exactly one document-level `keydown` listener exists across all surfaces.**
  Serves R16 (`SPEC.md`: "Neither slice registers a second document-level keydown listener").
  Edits both files.
  **Test:** spy on `document.addEventListener`, mount two surfaces, count calls whose first
  argument is `"keydown"`. **Property:** the count is exactly `1` with two surfaces open, and
  `document.removeEventListener` has been called for `"keydown"` once after both close.
  **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 10 passed (10)`. Cluster **C1**.

- **S02-S72 · The ADR for the shared modal-semantics boundary is written, as part of C1.**
  *(New in rework round 1 — orchestrator note on `t_3160e2d5`. Appended, so no existing step id
  moves.)*
  Serves R16 and R14 (the boundary those two requirements create) and §Is an ADR warranted?
  below. Creates `docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md`.
  **Operation:** the C1 coding seat TRANSCRIBES a decision that already exists in this plan —
  it decides nothing new. Sources, in this order: `DECISIONS.md`'s entries *"Who writes the ONE
  shared modal-semantics helper?"*, *"The Esc stack's implementation shape"* and *"The focus
  trap's focusable set"*; this file's §DDD and module boundaries → *Is an ADR warranted?*; and
  the exported-surface block at the head of §Cluster S02-C1.
  **Content, fixed so the step is not a judgement call:** `Status: Proposed` (V ratifies; no
  seat writes `Accepted`) · Context: seven existing `aria-modal` overlays with no focus trap,
  no Esc handling and no focus return, and `createPortal` / `Escape` / `focusTrap` / `.focus()`
  / `addEventListener("keydown"` at **0 hits** under `apps/ui` · Decision: one shared module
  `apps/ui/components/consent/modalSemantics.ts` owning focus trap, initial focus, focus
  return, backdrop close, `prefers-reduced-motion` and the Esc STACK, with the exported surface
  quoted verbatim from §Cluster S02-C1 · Consequences: S01 consumes it unchanged; ticket
  `A11Y-OVERLAYS` (`t_8962842f`) retrofits the seven existing overlays; exactly one
  `document`-level `keydown` listener exists across the app.
  **Acceptance — mechanical, and it adds no vitest case:**
  ```
  test -f docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md && echo EXISTS  -> EXISTS
  grep -c 'Status: Proposed' docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md -> 1
  for s in useModalSurface backdropCloseHandler prefersReducedMotion openSurfaceCount; do \
    grep -c "$s" docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md; done      -> each >= 1
  ```
  **C1's `Tests 10 passed (10)` and the C1 verification command are UNCHANGED by this step** —
  it writes no test, and the ADR path is outside every vitest filter.
  Cluster **C1**.
  **Why it is a step and not a note:** the plan and the packet already agreed the ADR is
  warranted, and an ADR nobody is told to write is an ADR nobody writes. It sits in C1 because
  C1 creates the module the ADR describes, and the two must not diverge.
  **Number `0022` is not invented, and it is not the next free id either — it is the
  orchestrator's allocation, and this paragraph is the CORRECTION of the number this plan
