### Cluster S02-C2 — the policy content module

Creates `apps/ui/lib/privacyPolicy.ts` and `tests/unit/consent-privacy-policy-data.test.ts`.
Pure data; no DOM, no token, no dependency on any other cluster. **Runs concurrently with C1.**

**The module's exported surface, fixed here:**

```ts
export type PolicyJump = Readonly<{ label: string; target: string }>;
export type PolicySection = Readonly<{
  no: string; title: string; accent: string; body: string; items: readonly string[];
}>;
export const POLICY_JUMP: readonly PolicyJump[];      // 8
export const POLICY_SECTIONS: readonly PolicySection[]; // 11
```
`accent` holds the CSS custom-property NAME without `var()` — e.g. `"--ok-dot"` — so the
component composes `var(${accent})` and the data file stays free of markup.

- **S02-S11 · The eight jump pills, in the design's own order, with their targets.**
  Serves R11, R20. Creates both files.
  **Test:** `POLICY_JUMP` deep-equals the eight records
  `CONTROLLER→policy-section-05 · WHAT WE COLLECT→policy-section-01 · LAWFUL BASIS→policy-section-06 ·
  PUBLISHING→policy-section-03 · MODELS & TRANSFERS→policy-section-04 · RETENTION→policy-section-07 ·
  YOUR GDPR RIGHTS→policy-section-08 · COMPLAINTS→policy-section-11`, **and**
  `POLICY_JUMP.map(p => p.label)` is NOT deep-equal to a sorted copy of itself.
  **Property:** the order is the design's (`design-data.js:51`) and has not been sorted into
  document order. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 1 passed (1)`. Cluster **C2**.

- **S02-S12 · Eleven sections, numbered `01`…`11`, titles in order.**
  Serves R12, R20. Edits both files.
  **Test:** `POLICY_SECTIONS.length === 11`; `.map(s => s.no)` equals `["01"…"11"]`;
  `.map(s => s.title)` equals the eleven titles of `SPEC.md` §Copy in order.
  **Property:** the section list is complete and ordered. **RED before, GREEN after.
  Acceptance:** `Tests 2 passed (2)`. Cluster **C2**.

- **S02-S13 · Bullet counts are exactly `[3,0,0,0,0,4,0,5,0,0,0]`, total 12.**
  Serves R12, R20. Edits both files.
  **Test:** `.map(s => s.items.length)` deep-equals that array and its sum is `12`.
  **Property:** only sections 01, 06 and 08 carry lists, with the counts the design gives.
  **Derivation of 12:** 3 + 4 + 5, the three list-bearing sections at `design-data.js:58-61`,
  `:67-72`, `:74-80`. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 3 passed (3)`.
  Cluster **C2**.

