### Cluster S02-C4 — the gate: the R17 mirror and the R18 handler refusal

Edits `apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx`; creates `tests/render/consent-signup-gate.test.tsx`;
edits `tests/render/auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` (ADDS one case). **Follows C3** (same file).

**Implementation shape, pinned by `SPEC.md` R17 and not open here:** both inputs stay
uncontrolled (no `checked` prop); each carries an `onChange` that mirrors
`event.currentTarget.checked` into a React boolean; those two booleans compute ONLY the submit
button's `disabled`; `FormData` stays the truth at submit.

**One qualification, added by the B1 correction and stated here because C4 is where the mirror
is written (`ARCH-REV-S02-r1` B1):** for `privacy-accepted`, "mirrors its
`event.currentTarget.checked`" means the **settled** value —
`event.currentTarget.checked && !event.nativeEvent.defaultPrevented`. C7's row handler cancels
that change, and mirroring the in-flight `true` records a state the DOM never reaches. Nothing
else in R17 moves: the inputs stay uncontrolled, the booleans still compute only `disabled`,
and `FormData` is still the truth at submit. `adult-affirmed`'s handler is the literal form.
The full mechanism, the measured handler ORDER it depends on, and the rejected alternatives are
in `§Cluster S02-C7` and in `DECISIONS.md`. **A C4 seat writes the guard on `privacy-accepted`
from the start; it is not a C7 edit to C4's work.**

**`SPEC.md` R17's six cases, in R17's own words — of which FOUR are in this cluster
(1, 2, 3, 6) and TWO are in `S02-C7` (4 and 5).** The N12 ruling (DECISIONS, 2026-09-06)
applies: R17's case text governs the two absolute sentences at `SPEC.md:356` and `:692`, and
cases 5 and 6 are written as R17 writes them.
**Cases 4 and 5 are the ONE place where R17's case text could not be followed literally**
(`ARCH-REV-S02-r2` **B3**; V-DECISIONS **V-18**): their ROUTE — a bare privacy `.click()` —
contradicts R05, which the same SPEC states and which V's goal requires. **The PROPERTY each
asserts is preserved exactly; only the route changes**, and the two steps are written out at
the end of `§Cluster S02-C7`. This is recorded, not repaired: `SPEC.md` is frozen
(md5 `ad060bda81db71f00f4c70b1dbf63f2f`) and stays so.
**Oracle, re-run by ARCH-S02 at authoring time**
(`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/v3-r17-cases-probe.mjs`, 6 cases × 4 implementation
variants × 3 runs, output pasted in §Clusters): all six PASS under the pinned variant; case 6
is RED under exactly the two controlled variants. **That oracle ran the R17 mirror ALONE, with
no row click rule — the stage this cluster leaves the component in — which is exactly why it
could not see B3.** The three-stage successor
(`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r2-r17-post-c7-fixed.mjs`) runs the
same six cases at the C4 stage, the C7 stage and the pre-B1-fix stage, and it is the oracle any
future edit to these six must re-run.

- **S02-S25 · Case 1 — neither box → `disabled`.**
  Serves R17. Creates `tests/render/consent-signup-gate.test.tsx`; edits the component.
  **Test:** fresh mount, no interaction. **Property:** the `Create account` button's `disabled`
  is `true`. **RED before** — today's button is `disabled={busy || sent}` and is therefore
  **enabled** at idle. **Text anchor, not a line number** (`ARCH-REV-S02-r1` N6; C3 edits this
  file above the button and moves it): the `<button className="authPrimary" type="submit"`
  element; count arm `grep -c 'className="authPrimary"' apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx` →
  `1`, measured at base `2b670d30` at `:190`. — **GREEN after. Acceptance:** the case passes.
  Cluster **C4**.

- **S02-S26 · Case 2 — only `adult-affirmed`, via `.click()` → `disabled`.**
  Serves R17. Edits both files.
  **Test:** `await act(async () => { field("adult-affirmed").click(); })`. **Property:** the
  button's `disabled` is still `true`. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** the case passes.
  Cluster **C4**.

- **S02-S27 · Case 3 — only `privacy-accepted`, via `.click()` → `disabled`.**
  Serves R17. Edits both files.
  **Test:** same idiom on the other input. **Property:** the button's `disabled` is still
  `true`. **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** the case passes. Cluster **C4**.
  **Note for the coding seat — invariance under C7, stated PER CASE and never as a
  generalisation (`ARCH-REV-S02-r2` **B3**).** At this point in the plan the privacy row's click
  still toggles the box natively; C7 is what makes it open the modal instead. Whether a case
  survives that change depends on the value it expects, so the six are split here and each row
  is measured
  (`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r2-r17-post-c7-fixed.mjs`, three
  stages × three runs, output in §Clusters):

  | case | step | clicks the privacy row? | expects | invariant under C7? |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | 1 | `S02-S25` | no interaction at all | `disabled=true` | **yes** |
  | 2 | `S02-S26` | clicks `adult-affirmed` only | `disabled=true` | **yes** |
  | 3 | `S02-S27` | **yes**, clicks the **input** | `disabled=true` | **yes** — the click is the same event either way and both paths leave the box unticked, so C7 adds no assertion that changes it |
  | 4 | `S02-S28` | **yes** | `disabled=FALSE` | **NO** — after C7 a bare click cannot tick the box, so the case is unsatisfiable as R17 words it. It is re-routed through the modal's acknowledgement and **lives in cluster C7**, at the end of §Cluster S02-C7 |
  | 5 | `S02-S29` | **yes**, in its second half | `disabled=FALSE` | **NO** — same mechanism, same re-route; its first half (assignment announces nothing) IS invariant |
  | 6 | `S02-S30` | **yes** | `disabled=true` | **yes** |

  **The rule this table encodes:** a C4 case that expects the button ENABLED cannot be reached
  without the modal, because after C7 the acknowledgement is the only route that ticks
  `privacy-accepted`. Cases 3 and 6 keep clicking the privacy row in this cluster precisely
  because they expect `disabled=true`, which both mechanisms produce.

**CASES 4 AND 5 ARE NOT IN THIS CLUSTER, and this is the one place the plan says so
(`ARCH-REV-S02-r2` **B3**; V-DECISIONS row **V-18**, default (a); DECISIONS entry
"R17 cases 4 and 5 vs R05").** Both expect `Create account` to be **enabled**, and after C7 the
only route to a ticked `privacy-accepted` is the modal's acknowledgement — which does not exist
until C7 wires the modal into `SignUpFlow.tsx`. Written as R17 words them they are green in C4
and RED in C7's own command, and C7 may not edit C4's test file (§Per-cluster boundaries), so a
C7 seat would be deadlocked by construction. Steps `S02-S28` and `S02-S29` therefore keep their
ids, keep the property R17 states, and are written out **at the end of §Cluster S02-C7**, in
`tests/render/consent-signup-modal.test.tsx`, which C7 creates and owns. **No step is
renumbered and no requirement loses a step:** the R17 trace row already reads `C4 · C7`.
**Consequence, stated because it is a real loss and not a wash:** `S02-S28` was C4's only
positive control, so `S02-C4`'s own command can no longer catch an implementation that
hard-codes `disabled` to `true`. That mutant is caught in `S02-C7` instead — by `S02-S28` in its
new home and, independently, by `S02-S53` — and C4's mutant-class row in §The cluster map now
says so rather than claiming a detection C4 no longer has.

- **S02-S30 · Case 6 — the pin that goes RED if a seat makes the inputs controlled.**
  Serves R17. Edits both files.
  **Test:** assign `.checked = true` on `adult-affirmed` only, WITHOUT dispatching; then
  `.click()` `privacy-accepted` inside `act` (that click is what forces a React re-render);
  then assert **both** that the button is still `disabled` **and that
  `field("adult-affirmed").checked` is still `true`**.
  **Property:** an uncontrolled input keeps an assigned value across a re-render; a controlled
  input is re-rendered from React state and reset to `false`. **The second assertion is the
  discriminating one** — measured green under all four variants without it.
  **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** the case passes, and it is measured RED under
  exactly the two controlled variants (the probe's matrix). Cluster **C4**.

