### Cluster S02-C7 — wiring the modal into the sign-up card

Edits `apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx`; creates `tests/render/consent-signup-modal.test.tsx`.
**Follows C3, C4, C5 and C6.**

**The one click rule for the privacy row, pinned by ARCH (DECISIONS 2026-09-06), stated once:**
one `onClick` on the row — if the box is CHECKED, do not `preventDefault`, and if the click did
not originate on the input call `input.click()` so the box unchecks through the path React
listens to, then return without opening anything; if it is UNCHECKED, `event.preventDefault()`
unconditionally and open the modal with `mode="consent"`.

**THE MIRROR RULE THAT MAKES THE CLICK RULE SAFE — the B1 correction
(ARCH-REV-S02-r1 B1; ARCH-S02-REWORK-R1, 2026-09-06). Read it with the click rule above; the
click rule alone is measured to ship a defect.** The class is *every place where the DOM
checkbox state and the R17 mirror can diverge*, and it has two members:

1. **Member 1 — the open path, and it is the load-bearing half.** `privacy-accepted`'s
   `onChange` mirrors the **settled** checked value, never the in-flight one:
   `setPrivacyMirror(event.currentTarget.checked && !event.nativeEvent.defaultPrevented)`.
   **Measured mechanism:** React 19.2.8 fires the ROW's `onClick` **before** the INPUT's
   `onChange`, and that `onChange` sees `currentTarget.checked === true` **and**
   `nativeEvent.defaultPrevented === true`, because jsdom's pre-click activation sets
   `.checked` before dispatch and its canceled-activation steps revert it *after* dispatch.
   Trace, verbatim: `onClick(mirror=false,domChecked=true) -> onChange(checked=true,defaultPrevented=true)`.
   The guard is correct precisely **because** the row handler runs first: by the time the
   mirror is written, `defaultPrevented` already records that this change will not happen.
   `adult-affirmed`'s `onChange` is unchanged (nothing ever cancels its change), so
   `SPEC.md` R17 point 2 is satisfied literally there and satisfied in substance here —
   see the DECISIONS entry for the frozen-text imprecision, recorded and not repaired.
2. **Member 2 — the dismissal paths, and it is defence in depth, labelled as such.** `×`,
   `Esc` and a backdrop click each resync the mirror from the DOM before closing:
   `setPrivacyMirror(privacyInputRef.current?.checked ?? false)`. **Measured: with member 1 in
   place this changes no observable outcome** (the `×`, `Esc` and backdrop routes end
   `DOM=false mirror=false btnDisabled=true` with and without it), so it is not sold as the
   fix. It is kept because it makes invariant 2 structural instead of accidental: the mirror
   cannot outlive the DOM across a close, whatever a later edit does to the open path.

**Why the verdict's own first wording is NOT what is pinned here, measured:** driving the
mirror to `false` inside the row handler (`setPrivacyMirror(false)` beside `preventDefault()`)
**does not work** — the `onChange` runs *after* it and overwrites it with `true`. Measured over
8 routes: it still desyncs on open-by-square and still lets two clicks reach `register()`.
Full matrix and the three rejected alternatives are in `DECISIONS.md`
(`### Rework round 1 — ARCH-REV-S02-r1's verdict, applied`).

**THE MIRROR ARM, added by the B1 correction to all six route steps below
(`S02-S49`, `S02-S50`, `S02-S51`, `S02-S54`, `S02-S55`, `S02-S56`). Written out once, and each
step names it rather than restating it — two formulations of one rule is the B4 defect class.**

> **Mirror arm:** after the route under test, `await act(async () => { field("adult-affirmed").click(); })`
> and assert the `Create account` button's `disabled` is **still `true`**.
>
> **Why the extra click is the whole point:** `disabled` is computed from *both* mirrors, so
> with `adult-affirmed` false the button is disabled whatever the privacy mirror says. Ticking
> `adult-affirmed` is what makes the privacy mirror the only remaining term — so a desynced
> `true` shows up as an ENABLED button and the assertion fails. Without this click the step
> asserts nothing about the mirror. **Measured against the defect it exists to catch:** on the
> unfixed rule the square route and the `×` route end `mirror=true btnDisabled=false`; on the
> pinned rule all six end `mirror=false btnDisabled=true`
> (`.hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r1-c7-mirror-fixed.mjs`, three runs).
> **It uses the ONE button idiom** (`field(name).click()` inside `await act`), never an
> assignment.

- **S02-S49 · Clicking the unchecked check SQUARE opens the modal; box and mirror stay `false`.**
  Serves R05, and R17's mirror invariant. Creates the test file; edits the component.
  **Test:** `.click()` the `privacy-accepted` input, **then the mirror arm above**.
  **Property:** a `[role="dialog"]` is in the document, `field("privacy-accepted").checked === false`,
  and after `field("adult-affirmed").click()` the `Create account` button is still `disabled`.
  **RED before** (today the click ticks the box and opens nothing; and against the *pre-B1* rule
  the third assertion is the one that fails — `disabled` is `false`), **GREEN after.
  Acceptance:** `Tests 1 passed (1)`. Cluster **C7**.

- **S02-S50 · Clicking the row's TEXT does the same.**
  Serves R05, R17. Edits both files.
  **Test:** `.click()` the row-2 text span, **then the mirror arm**. **Property:** dialog
  present, box still `false`, button still `disabled` after the mirror arm.
  **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 2 passed (2)`. Cluster **C7**.

- **S02-S51 · Clicking the `Privacy Policy` control does the same.**
  Serves R05, R17. Edits both files.
  **Test:** `.click()` the `<button type="button">` whose text is `Privacy Policy`,
  **then the mirror arm**. **Property:** dialog present, box still `false`, button still
  `disabled` after the mirror arm.
  **RED before, GREEN after. Acceptance:** `Tests 3 passed (3)`. Cluster **C7**.
  **This is the single most likely implementation slip in the slice** (`SPEC.md` R05) — all
  three entry points are pinned separately for that reason, and a `preventDefault` that covers
  only one of them fails exactly one of these three cases.

- **S02-S52 · Clicking the CHECKED privacy row unchecks it directly, with no modal.**
  Serves R06. Edits both files.
  **Test:** reach the checked state through the modal path (open, satisfy the gate, click
