ROUTE to the "both boxes checked" state changes: the modal's acknowledgement instead of a bare
privacy `.click()`, because after the click rule above a bare click cannot tick the box. **The
acknowledgement route, written out once so neither step restates it** (two formulations of one
rule is the B4 class):

> **Acknowledgement route:** `await act(async () => { field("privacy-accepted").click(); })` to
> open the policy in `mode="consent"`; drive the scroll region's metrics to a scrolled-to-end
> state with `Object.defineProperty(region, "scrollTop"|"clientHeight"|"scrollHeight",
> { value, configurable: true })` and dispatch one `scroll` event, so `S02-S40`'s gate
> (`scrollTop + clientHeight >= scrollHeight - 8`) latches; assert the `I have read it` control
> is **no longer `disabled`**; then `.click()` it inside `act`. **Post-conditions asserted by
> both steps:** `field("privacy-accepted").checked === true` and no `[role="dialog"]` remains.
