Round 1's C9 column claimed the mutant *"the merge losing S01's or S02's `globals.css` block"*
against a command that could not detect it. It can now, and the claim is measured rather than
asserted.

**PART 5 — the THREE standing gates, now MECHANICAL commands with their own mutants**
(`COMMON.md` §10.18 hit-list counting, §10.19 sub-command exit codes, §10.20 reported and not
folded). Round 1 stated these as prose deltas; a prose delta cannot be run three times.

```
      G1 raw   : generateExit=0 typecheckExit=1 tscRan=1 s14=8 all=8
      G1 terms: generateExit=0 tscRanFingerprint=1 diagnosticsElsewhere=0 | s14Total=8 (reported, NOT asserted)
   G1 VERDICT=0   (the DELTA holds)
   mutants:  a diagnostic OUTSIDE the pinned file       -> 1
             typecheck never ran (no fingerprint line)  -> 1
             generate:contract never ran (exit 127)     -> 1
             the OTHER mission REPAIRS its 8 (s14 -> 0) -> 0   <- the guard MUST survive this

      G2 terms: exit=1 FAILlines=2 toggleNamed=1 literalNamed=1 hitList=1 pinnedHit=1
   G2 VERDICT=0   (named-failure-set delta + hit-list count, both anchored on ASCII)
   mutants:  a THIRD test fails -> 1
             a SECOND colour literal (hit list 2) -> 1
             the PINNED hit silently vanished -> 1
             a DIFFERENT test failed instead of the toggle -> 1
             the file went green, i.e. the pin itself disappeared -> 1

S02-G3 | vt=0 VERDICT=0 | brokenSigs=0 cannotFindModule=0 noTestFiles=0
S02-G3 | Tests    :       Tests  2 passed (2)
S02-G3 | TestFiles:  Test Files  1 passed (1)
   G3 VERDICT=0   (green at base, so the ordinary guard applies unchanged)
```

**G1 is in the MONOTONE-DELTA form, and that is a correction to round 0.** `TOOLING-TRAPS.md`
("assert what must not appear, never what must remain broken"): a guard that asserts the pinned
diagnostic TOTAL is asserting **another mission's number**, and it goes red the day that mission
repairs its own file — a guard that fails on someone else's SUCCESS. So the three asserted arms
are (a) `generate:contract` exited `0`, (b) **`tsc` actually ran** — `grep -cE '^\$ tsc --noEmit$'`
is `1`, which is the fingerprint that stops a run that never happened from passing vacuously
(`COMMON.md` §10.19), and (c) **zero** diagnostics outside `tests/unit/s14-ui.test.ts`. The
total (`8`) is **printed and not asserted**, and the last mutant above proves the difference:
the guard stays green when the other mission drops to `0`. **G2 keeps its exact-count form
because `COMMON.md` §10.12 and §10.18 require it there** (the named-failure-set must be exactly
the pinned set, and the hit list must be exactly the baseline count plus the pinned element) —
these are this mission's own pins on its own file, not another mission's number.

**G2's two named failures, quoted so the anchor is checkable:**
`tests/unit/t9-mode-tokens.test.ts > T9-C3 mode control and document guard > renders one accessible toggle that reads the document mode, flips it, and persists it`
and `… > leaves no mode-inert colour literal in the four Wave-0 product files`.
**The hit-list arm counts the received ARRAY's elements** (`^\+ +"/.*:[0-9]+:`), not the `FAIL`
line: a second offending colour literal adds an array element and changes neither the `FAIL`
count nor the summary, so counting failures alone would miss it (`COMMON.md` §10.18). The
pinned element is asserted separately so it cannot silently vanish. All three gates match
`BASELINE.md`. **G1 and G2 are RED for their pinned, inherited reasons — a seat reports the
delta, never the word "green".**

