### The R17 oracle, re-run by ARCH-S02 at authoring time

`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/v3-r17-cases-probe.mjs`, React 19.2.8 / jsdom 30.0.1,
6 cases × 4 implementation variants × 3 runs, **all three runs identical**. Run 3 verbatim:

```
  case                                                                      A   B   C   D
  case 1  neither box -> disabled                                           PASS  PASS  PASS  PASS
  case 2  only adult-affirmed via click() -> disabled                       PASS  PASS  PASS  PASS
  case 3  only privacy-accepted via click() -> disabled                     PASS  PASS  PASS  PASS
  case 4  both via click() -> NOT disabled                                  PASS  PASS  PASS  PASS
  case 5  assign true both/no dispatch -> disabled; reset false; click both -> enables PASS  PASS  PASS  PASS
  case 6  assign adult only/no dispatch; click privacy; adult .checked STILL true + still disabled PASS  RED   PASS  RED
  legend: A=uncontrolled+FormData (pinned)  B=controlled+mirror  C=uncontrolled+mirror  D=controlled+FormData
```

**What this buys the six steps `S02-S25`…`S02-S30`:** the controlled-inputs guarantee lives on
case 6 and nowhere else (RED under exactly B and D). A coding seat that finds case 5 detecting
nothing has not found a defect — that is measured and recorded.

**What it does NOT buy, and this is `ARCH-REV-S02-r2` B3.** This oracle's four variants all
carry the R17 mirror **and no row click rule** — the component as `S02-C4` leaves it. Under
that component a bare privacy `.click()` ticks the box, so cases 4 and 5 pass. They do not
survive `S02-C7`, which is where the click rule and the B1 mirror correction land, and since
round 1 the N7 chain rule puts `consent-signup-gate.test.tsx` inside **C7's own** verification
command. **"All six PASS under the pinned variant" was true of the stage it was measured at and
false of the finished component, and the plan carried it as if it were unconditional.**

### The three-stage R17 oracle — the successor probe, and B3's discharge

Any future edit to R17's six cases re-runs THIS one, not only the four-variant matrix above: it
is the one that runs the cases against the component at more than one stage.

`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r2-r17-post-c7-fixed.mjs`,
React 19.2.8 / jsdom 30.0.1, **three invocations, all identical**, corrected case-4/case-5
route. Run 3 verbatim:

```
===== STAGE c4 =====
  PASS  S02-S25 case1 neither          -> expect disabled=true 
  PASS  S02-S26 case2 only adult       -> expect disabled=true 
  PASS  S02-S27 case3 only privacy     -> expect disabled=true 
  FAIL  S02-S28 case4 BOTH via the modal ack -> expect disabled=FALSE  ERROR:NO MODAL AT THIS STAGE — the acknowledgement route does not exist until C7 wires the modal into SignUpFlow; this case cannot live in cluster C4
  FAIL  S02-S29 case5 assign,reset,modal ack -> expect disabled=FALSE  ERROR:NO MODAL AT THIS STAGE — the acknowledgement route does not exist until C7 wires the modal into SignUpFlow; this case cannot live in cluster C4
  PASS  S02-S30 case6 assign adult,click privacy -> disabled=true+adult stays true
  ---- STAGE c4: 4/6 pass, 2 FAIL

===== STAGE c7 =====
  PASS  S02-S25 case1 neither          -> expect disabled=true 
  PASS  S02-S26 case2 only adult       -> expect disabled=true 
  PASS  S02-S27 case3 only privacy     -> expect disabled=true 
  PASS  S02-S28 case4 BOTH via the modal ack -> expect disabled=FALSE
  PASS  S02-S29 case5 assign,reset,modal ack -> expect disabled=FALSE
  PASS  S02-S30 case6 assign adult,click privacy -> disabled=true+adult stays true
  ---- STAGE c7: 6/6 pass, 0 FAIL

===== STAGE c7-unfixed =====
  ---- STAGE c7-unfixed: 6/6 pass, 0 FAIL
```

**Read the two stage lines together — they are the whole of B3's remedy.** `STAGE c7: 6/6 pass`
is the discharge: the corrected cases are satisfiable against the finished component.
`STAGE c4: 4/6 pass` with `NO MODAL AT THIS STAGE` is the reason they had to leave C4: the
acknowledgement is the only lawful route to a ticked `privacy-accepted`, and it does not exist
until C7. **`STAGE c7-unfixed` no longer discriminates** (6/6) and is retained only as the
reviewer's contrast control — under the corrected route the desync is not what makes the cases
pass, which is precisely the property that was missing before.

**The RED control, the reviewer's own probe left byte-untouched, run in the same session:**

```
$ node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-rev-s02-r2-r17-post-c7.mjs
  ---- STAGE c4: 6/6 pass, 0 FAIL
  ---- STAGE c7: 4/6 pass, 2 FAIL
  ---- STAGE c7-unfixed: 6/6 pass, 0 FAIL
```

