### The jsdom facts behind `S02-S08`, `S02-S40`…`S02-S43` and `S02-S48`, run by ARCH-S02

```
jsdom 30.0.1
M2 typeof window.matchMedia : undefined
M3 default scrollTop/clientHeight/scrollHeight : 0 0 0
M3 after defineProperty                       : 0 200 500
M3 redefine scrollTop=292 -> reached? (292+200>=500-8): true
M3 redefine scrollTop=291 -> reached? (291+200>=500-8): false
M3 typeof el.scrollIntoView                   : undefined
M3 typeof el.focus / document.activeElement   : function BODY
```

**Two of these would have cost a coding round each:** an unguarded `window.matchMedia` call
throws in every render test that mounts the modal, and an unguarded `scrollIntoView` throws on
every pill click. Both now have a guarded shape pinned in `S02-S08` and `S02-S48`.

A cluster is the smallest group of steps verifiable together, independently of the rest of the
slice. It is also the review unit: a reviewer probes a cluster, never a whole-slice diff. The
`mutant class` column names the defect the cluster's command would catch if introduced —
a cluster whose command passes under its own mutant is not a verification.

## DDD and module boundaries (ARCH-S02)

### Bounded contexts this slice touches

| Context | What S02 does in it | Who else is in it |
|---|---|---|
| **Registration** (`apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx`, `packages/contract`) | Adds a second pre-condition to the *local* act of registering. **Adds nothing to the request.** `client.register(email, password, recoveryEmail, adultAffirmed)` keeps four positional arguments (`packages/contract/src/client.ts:215-220`). | `apps/api`, `migrations`, the contract package — **all read-only for this mission**. |
| **Policy content** (`apps/ui/lib/privacyPolicy.ts`, new) | Introduces the policy as **data**: two frozen exported constants, transcribed from the design. No component, no storage, no network. | Nobody. This module is new and S02 is its only writer. |
| **Modal semantics** (`apps/ui/components/consent/modalSemantics.ts`, new) | Introduces the mission's one behavioural boundary: focus trap, initial focus, focus return, backdrop close, reduced-motion, **and the Esc stack**. | **S01 consumes it unchanged**; ticket `A11Y-OVERLAYS` (`t_8962842f`) will later retrofit seven existing overlays onto it. |
| **Consent surfaces** (`apps/ui/components/consent/`) | Owns `PrivacyPolicyModal.tsx` and `modalSemantics.ts`. | **S01 owns everything else in that directory**, including `apps/ui/lib/consent.ts` and the browser-local consent preferences. |
| **Browser-local consent preferences** (`localStorage['debateai.consent']`) | **S02 does not enter this context at all.** It reads and writes no storage, and `SignUpFlow.tsx` may not even contain the substring `localStorage` (R21, enforced by `authRoutes.source-test.mjs:48`). | S01 alone. |

### Invariants S02 owns

1. **The privacy box is ticked only through the modal's acknowledgement.** Every other route —
   a click on the unchecked square, text or link; `×`; `Esc`; a backdrop click — leaves it
   `false`. Pinned by `S02-S49`…`S02-S51`, `S02-S54`…`S02-S56`.
2. **The DOM is the truth at submit; React state is the truth for the button.** `FormData` is
   read for the refusal (`S02-S31`); the mirror computes only `disabled` (`S02-S25`…`S02-S30`).
   Violating this in either direction breaks a measured test: reading the mirror at submit takes
   `auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` from 18 to 15; controlling the inputs turns `S02-S30` red.
3. **Exactly one surface acts on one `Escape`, and it is the topmost.** Owned by
   `modalSemantics.ts`, pinned at the mechanism (`S02-S01`) and at both consumers (`S02-S56`).
4. **Exactly one `document`-level `keydown` listener exists across both slices**
   (`S02-S10`).
5. **The modal owns no consent state and reads or writes no storage** — it is prop-driven, and
   `onAcknowledge` fires only from `I have read it` and only in `mode="consent"` (`S02-S39`,
   `S02-S47`).
6. **The scroll gate latches.** Once satisfied it never re-closes (`S02-S41`).
7. **Every colour S02 ships is a `var(--token)` reference** (`S02-S60`) — which is what makes
   invariant 8 free.
8. **Both surfaces follow `html[data-mode]` with nothing wired** (R23).

### Domain terms this slice introduces

`consent group` (the bordered two-row box) · `consent row` · `privacy acceptance` (the local,
un-transmitted fact, distinct from `adult affirmation`, which IS transmitted) · `policy jump`
(a pill) · `policy section` · `scroll-to-end gate` · `acknowledgement` (the only tick path) ·
`modal surface` (a registration in the Esc stack) · `Esc stack` (topmost consumes).

### What S02 must NOT touch

`apps/api/**` · `packages/**` (the registration request keeps its exact shape, R19) ·
`migrations/**` · `tools/**` · `apps/runner/**` · `apps/scheduler/**` · MFA / verify-email /
login / recovery flows · `tests/unit/registration*.test.ts` · `tests/integration/**` · **both
`globals.css` token blocks and `tests/unit/t9-mode-tokens.test.ts` (S01 is their sole writer)**
· `apps/ui/app/layout.tsx` · `apps/ui/app/settings/page.tsx` · `apps/ui/components/AuthShell.tsx`
· `apps/ui/lib/consent.ts` and every other S01-owned file under `apps/ui/components/consent/` ·
the retrofit of the seven existing overlays (ticket `A11Y-OVERLAYS`, `t_8962842f`) ·
`apps/ui/scripts/node-test-manifest.json` (**not needed — S02 adds no `*.source-test.mjs`;
DECISIONS records when it would be**).

### Is an ADR warranted?

**Yes, for `modalSemantics.ts`. It is not written by the ARCHITECTURE seat — it is written by
the C1 CODING seat, as step `S02-S72`, and the path is fixed:
`docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md`, status `Proposed` (V
ratifies).** *(Rework round 1: round 0 named this an unnumbered `ADR-0NN` with no step and no
owner, which is an ADR nobody writes. The orchestrator's note on `t_3160e2d5` allocated the
number and the owner; `S02-S72` carries the acceptance arms and the id measurement.)* The
Esc-stack rule — *the
topmost open surface consumes Esc and no other surface acts on the same event* — is law for
every future overlay in this repo, not for these two: `A11Y-OVERLAYS` (`t_8962842f`) exists
precisely to retrofit seven existing `aria-modal` overlays onto it, and today
`createPortal`/`Escape`/`focusTrap`/`.focus()`/`addEventListener("keydown"` return **0 hits**
under `apps/ui`. That is a new repo-wide boundary and it outlives the mission, which is the
ADR test. Creating the file is outside the ARCHITECTURE seat's `allowed` list; this paragraph
plus the DECISIONS lines is what `S02-S72` transcribes, and no seat decides anything new there.

Nothing else here warrants one: the policy data module and the two components are mission-local
and die with the slice's file surface.

