reviewed commit. No push, no merge, no Done — V performs every merge and every Done.

### Per-cluster boundaries (ARCH-S02) — each row IS the coding seat's `allowed` list

A seat dispatched on a cluster may write the files in its row and nothing else. Every file not
in its row is forbidden to it, including files another S02 cluster owns.

**RUNNING a test file is not WRITING it — stated because the chain rule (`ARCH-REV-S02-r1` N7)
now puts other clusters' test files inside `C4`'s, `C6`'s, `C7`'s and `C9`'s verification
commands.** Those files are **read-only** to the seat: if an earlier cluster's test goes red,
that is a finding against the current seat's change, and the remedy is to fix the change — never
to edit the earlier test. A seat that believes the earlier test is itself wrong files a finding
and stops (`heartbeat-protocol` §2.7). The `allowed` column below is unchanged by the chain
rule and remains the write surface.

| Cluster | `allowed` (exhaustive) | `forbidden` beyond the slice-level list above |
|---|---|---|
| **S02-C1** | `apps/ui/components/consent/modalSemantics.ts` (create) · `tests/render/consent-modal-semantics.test.tsx` (create) · **`docs/architecture/01-decisions/ADR-0022-shared-modal-semantics.md` (create — `S02-S72`, status `Proposed`; V ratifies)** | `SignUpFlow.tsx` · `PrivacyPolicyModal.tsx` · `privacyPolicy.ts` · `globals.css` · `auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` · every other ADR in `docs/architecture/01-decisions/`, including S01's `ADR-0019-consent-storage-contract.md` |
| **S02-C2** | `apps/ui/lib/privacyPolicy.ts` (create) · `tests/unit/consent-privacy-policy-data.test.ts` (create) | everything C1 and C3-C8 own |
| **S02-C3** | `apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx` · `tests/render/consent-signup-group.test.tsx` (create) · `tests/render/auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` (**three inserted lines, one after each occurrence of `field("adult-affirmed").checked = true;`, identified by the three `it(...)` titles listed in `S02-S22`; count arms `3`/`3`. `S02-S22` is the authoritative statement of this edit — the numbers this row used to carry (`:324`, `:448`, `:466`) were pre-edit positions that shift as soon as the first line is inserted, which is `ARCH-REV-S02-r1` N6 and was carried over as `ARCH-REV-S02-r2` N6**) | `globals.css` · both consent components · `privacyPolicy.ts` |
| **S02-C4** | `apps/ui/components/SignUpFlow.tsx` · `tests/render/consent-signup-gate.test.tsx` (create) · `tests/render/auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` (**one added case and nothing else**) | as C3, **plus `tests/render/consent-signup-group.test.tsx`, which C4's command RUNS and C4 may not WRITE** |
| **S02-C5** | `apps/ui/components/consent/PrivacyPolicyModal.tsx` (create) · `tests/render/consent-policy-modal-render.test.tsx` (create) | `modalSemantics.ts` (**consume it; if it needs a change, that is a finding against C1, not an edit here**) · `privacyPolicy.ts` (same rule) · `SignUpFlow.tsx` · `globals.css` |
